- How would you handle skewed category distributions and ensure stability during microbursts?
- What are the trade-offs of using a single global heap vs per-category heaps for top-K queries?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about DAGs, timing, and dynamic programming over graphs, a common pattern in build pipelines, data workflows, or task scheduling.

## Key Concepts

- Topological sort to linearize a DAG
- DP on DAG to propagate earliest start times
- In-degree based BFS (Kahn) and cycle detection

## Code Example

```javascript
function earliestTimes(n, duration, edges) {
  const g = Array.from({length: n}, () => []);
  const indeg = Array(n).fill(0);
  for (const [u, v] of edges) { g[u].push(v); indeg[v]++; }
  const es = Array(n).fill(0);
  const q = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  let visited = 0;
  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    visited++;
    for (const v of g[u]) {
      es[v] = Math.max(es[v], es[u] + duration[u]);
      if (--indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
    }
  }
  const total = Math.max(...es.map((s, i) => s + duration[i]));
  return { earliestStart: es, totalDuration: total };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt to detect cycles and report the cycle path?
- How would you extend to handle parallel resources or varying durations per edge?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess understanding of Trie data structure and practical prefix search used in autocompletion; tests familiarity with basic data structures and iteration over strings.

## Key Concepts
- Trie structure with 26-way children
- insert/search/startsWith time complexity O(m)
- memory proportional to number of unique prefixes

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode { constructor(){ this.next = new Array(26).fill(null); this.end=false; } }
class Trie { constructor(){ this.root = new TrieNode(); }
 insert(word){ let p=this.root; for(let ch of word){ let idx=ch.charCodeAt(0)-97; if(!p.next[idx]) p.next[idx]=new TrieNode(); p=p.next[idx]; } p.end=true; }
 search(word){ let p=this.root; for(let ch of word){ let idx=ch.charCodeAt(0)-97; if(!p.next[idx]) return false; p=p.next[idx]; } return p.end; }
 startsWith(prefix){ let p=this.root; for(let ch of prefix){ let idx=ch.charCodeAt(0)-97; if(!p.next[idx]) return false; p=p.next[idx]; } return true; }
}
```

